PDC EXPERIMENT 7 — CORBA WITH JAVA IDL
======================================

AIM
---
Develop a distributed calculator application using CORBA and Java IDL.

REQUIREMENTS
------------
Java 8
IDL compiler: idlj
Naming Service: tnameserv
Three terminal windows

EXECUTION STEPS
---------------

1. Open Ubuntu WSL.

2. Enter the project folder:

cd /mnt/f/BTech/PDC/Exam/7/CORBAExperiment

3. Generate Java files from IDL (if needed):

idlj -fall Calculator.idl

4. Compile generated files:

javac CalculatorApp/*.java

5. Compile application files:

javac CalculatorImpl.java CalculatorServer.java CalculatorClient.java

6. TERMINAL 1 — Start Naming Service:

tnameserv -ORBInitialPort 1050

Keep running.

7. TERMINAL 2 — Start Server:

java CalculatorServer -ORBInitialPort 1050

Expected: Calculator Server Ready...

Keep running.

8. TERMINAL 3 — Start Client:

java CalculatorClient -ORBInitialPort 1050

EXPECTED OUTPUT
---------------
Addition = 30
Subtraction = 10
Multiplication = 200
Division = 2.0

IMPORTANT TERMS
---------------
CORBA = Common Object Request Broker Architecture
ORB = Object Request Broker
IDL = Interface Definition Language
POA = Portable Object Adapter
Stub = Client-side remote-object representative
Naming Service = Finds the remote object
idlj = Generates Java bindings from IDL
tnameserv = Starts the Naming Service

REMEMBER
--------
Server: Create -> Register -> Wait
Client: Find -> Call -> Display

Run the Naming Service first, then the server, then the client.